cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuantJulia in research, please cite it as below."
title: "QuantJulia: differentiable option pricing and rough-volatility calibration in Julia"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Yugam2508
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yugam2508/QuantJulia"
url: "https://yugam2508.github.io/QuantJulia/dev/"
abstract: >-
  A Julia library for option pricing and volatility-model calibration with
  automatic differentiation throughout. It covers Black-Scholes, Heston, rough
  Heston (fractional Riccati solver), lifted Heston, rough Bergomi and jump
  models; Fourier (Gil-Pelaez, COS) and reproducible multithreaded Monte Carlo
  pricing; SVI/SSVI and Dupire local volatility; American, barrier and Asian
  options; yield curves and cash dividends; and calibration diagnostics. It is
  cross-validated against QuantLib, and includes a study showing that the ATM
  skew power law does not identify the Hurst exponent of rough Heston.
keywords:
  - option pricing
  - rough volatility
  - Heston model
  - calibration
  - automatic differentiation
  - Monte Carlo
  - Julia
